# which button supports which pattern (UIF-1430, UIF-1431)
ok Plain: GetPatternProvider 10000 returns S_OK
ok a plain button: Invoke
ok Plain: GetPatternProvider 10015 returns S_OK
ok a plain button: no Toggle
ok Drop: GetPatternProvider 10000 returns S_OK
ok a drop-down button: Invoke
ok Drop: GetPatternProvider 10015 returns S_OK
ok a drop-down button: no Toggle
ok Check: GetPatternProvider 10015 returns S_OK
ok a check button: Toggle
ok Check: GetPatternProvider 10000 returns S_OK
ok a check button: no Invoke
ok Separator: GetPatternProvider 10000 returns S_OK
ok a separator: no Invoke
ok Separator: GetPatternProvider 10015 returns S_OK
ok a separator: no Toggle
ok Plain: GetPatternProvider 10002 returns S_OK
ok a plain button: no other pattern
# Invoke (UIF-1430)
ok Off: GetPatternProvider 10000 returns S_OK
ok a disabled button: refused
ok OnOffBar: GetPatternProvider 10000 returns S_OK
ok a button on a disabled tool bar: refused
ok a refused Invoke clicks nothing
ok Plain: GetPatternProvider 10000 returns S_OK
ok an enabled button: S_OK
ok Invoke returns before OnClick runs (the click is posted)
ok OnClick runs once the posted message is handled
ok and only once
ok Drop: GetPatternProvider 10000 returns S_OK
ok a drop-down button: S_OK
ok a drop-down button clicks as well
# Toggle (UIF-1431)
ok Check: GetPatternProvider 10015 returns S_OK
ok get_ToggleState returns S_OK
ok up: Off
ok Toggle: S_OK
ok Toggle returns before the click (posted)
ok the posted click puts it down
ok OnClick ran once
ok get_ToggleState returns S_OK
ok down: On
ok a second Toggle releases it
ok get_ToggleState returns S_OK
ok Down set by the program: On
ok get_ToggleState returns S_OK
ok released by the program: Off
ok OffCheck: GetPatternProvider 10015 returns S_OK
ok a disabled check button: refused
ok a refused Toggle changes nothing
# a button freed before its posted click (UIF-1425, UIF-1427)
ok Gone: GetPatternProvider 10000 returns S_OK
ok Invoke: S_OK
ok no click after the button is gone
